text:
I bought this to replace my 25 1/2 year old Weber Spirit, which had most of the guts replaced at least once , but the frame was rusting.
LIKES- the lid and the way it opens flush to the wall;
           -the electric starter;
           - the swing down side table.
DISLIKES- that it was made in China;
                - the gas knobs!*some of this is my fault , but read on..
 The new Spirit knobs turn counter-clockwise. in my first 3 uses i had all knobs turned fully on , and the temp never exceeded 400. Strange. Then i saw it. The 3 o'clock and final position is actually 25%! there is a small circle at that position which has a 25% piece of pie. The 9 o'clock and first position is full on. Well this is counter-intuitive. When i turn on a faucet , the more i turn the more water i get. I wrote to three friends who purchased Webers this year. TWO of them had the same complaint-- not hot enough! the third , an engineer, figured it out by the sound of the gas being released. The other two thought this low fire was a "new normal" and they now get it. and by the way , my old Spirit knobs worked clockwise, no markings - just the more you turned it , the more gas was dispensed.
I suggest Weber label the thing "HI, MED, LO" - you know , an American thing!

I have shopped for a while for a grill that is well built, cooks even, and I don't need a loan to buy.   After much research, this is the one I went with.  For context, I normally cook for 5-8 people, and I am grilling 2-3 times a week year around.  I have had this for about a month.

The Great:  Weber Customer Service - i had a problem, they made it right immediately

The good:  grill even-ness front to back and side to side is wonderful;  overall sturdy & well made; easy to put together;  really like the gas gauge;  it has really improved my cooking game; I like the fold down side;  access to grease tray from front;  thermometer on lid is accurate;

A little below expectations: temperature consistency on long low grills had almost a 30 deg variation;  the low setting is more of a medium, so with one burner on low, i can't get below 200 deg;  the spot for the iGrill is not magnetic, making it useless;  wish both sides folded down;  

Overall:   The best grill I have used in this price range, although i wish it was a little bigger

The grill works well overall. My two areas I'd like to see improved are; 

1. If you don't want to buy a cover, the grease drip tray collects water
2. The propane tank level gauge movement isn't very reliable.
